## QUESTION : CACHE HIT vs CACHE MISS ?
------------------------------------------

### CACHE HIT : 
---------------

Jab requested data Cache me successfully mil jaata hai. 
Application directly Cache se data retrieve karke response
return kar deti hai — Database hit nahi hota.

### CACHE MISS : 
----------------

Jab requested data Cache me available nahi hota. 
Application Database se data retrieve karti hai, 
future requests ke liye Cache me store karti hai,
aur phir response return karti hai.



=====================================================
# QUESTION : CACHE DATABASE SE TEZ KYUN HOTA HAI ? 
=====================================================

- Cache implementations (jaise Redis) data ko primarily RAM me store karte hain jo ki
  fast-access memory hai. Iske comparison me Database ka persistent storage disk (SSD/HDD)
  par hota hai, jo RAM se significantly slower hai (Waise kuch cache implementations disk 
  persistence bhi support karti hain — mainly data recovery/durability ke liye.)

- Database apni performance improve karne ke liye frequently accessed data aur index pages
  ko apne Buffer Pool (RAM) me cache karta hai. Lekin agar required data Buffer Pool me nahi hai,
  to Database use dobara disk se fetch karta hai — jisse additional I/O latency aati hai.
  Saath hi, Database query process karne me additional overhead bhi hota hai — jaise CPU computation, 
  aur Application ↔ DB network call.




