## REPLICATION DELAY
---------------------

Primary Node par hone wale updates ya invalidations Redis ke internal
replication mechanism ke through associated Replicas tak propagate hote hain.

Primary aur Replicas ke beech replication me thoda delay ho sakta hai.

Example:

Primary  → Price = ₹120
Replica 1 → Price = ₹120
Replica 2 → Price = ₹100

Agar isi time read request Replica 2 ke paas route ho jaaye, to
temporarily stale data return ho sakta hai.

### TRADE-OFF:
Read traffic multiple Redis Nodes me distribute kiya ja sakta hai,
lekin replication delay ki wajah se temporary stale reads possible hain.


## READ REPLICAS KAB USEFUL HAIN?
----------------------------------

Read Replicas especially useful hoti hain jab:

- Kisi particular Redis Node par read traffic bahut high ho. Ye ek Hot Key ki wajah se ho sakta hai, ya multiple Hot Keys ki combined read traffic ki wajah se.
- Temporary stale data acceptable ho, kyunki replication delay ki wajah se Replicas kabhi-kabhi temporarily outdated data return kar sakti hain.



