Load Balancer request ko kisi ek Application Instance ke paas route
karta hai.

Maan lo request Application Instance 3 ke paas jaati hai.

Application ko pata hai ki `product:101` ki `N = 3` cached copies
maintain ki jaati hain.

Application `1` se `N` ke beech ek random number generate karke
ek cache copy select karti hai.

Maan lo:

Random Number = 2

Isliye selected cache key hogi:

product:101:2

Application is key ko Redis Cluster se fetch karne ke liye request
bhejti hai.

Redis Client key ka hash calculate karke corresponding Hash Slot
determine karta hai aur slot-to-node mapping ke basis par request ko
appropriate Redis Node tak route karta hai.

Lekin kyunki update ke baad sabhi cache copies invalidate kar di gayi
thi:

product:101:2 → Cache Miss

Application latest product data Database se fetch karti hai:

Database
↓
product:101
↓
{iPhone, ₹120}

Ab Application ko latest data mil gaya hai.

Kyuki Application ko pata hai ki `product:101` ek Hot Key hai aur iski
`N = 3` cached copies maintain karni hain, Application multiple cache
copies dobara create karti hai:

SET product:101:1 {iPhone, ₹120}
SET product:101:2 {iPhone, ₹120}
SET product:101:3 {iPhone, ₹120}

Redis Client har key ka hash calculate karke corresponding Hash Slot
determine karta hai.

Slot-to-node mapping ke basis par har cache write request appropriate
Redis Node tak route ki jaati hai aur corresponding cache copy wahan
store kar di jaati hai.

Ab Redis Cluster me latest product data ki multiple independent cached
copies available hain:

product:101:1 → {iPhone, ₹120}
product:101:2 → {iPhone, ₹120}
product:101:3 → {iPhone, ₹120}

Finally, Application Database se fetched latest product data Client ko
return kar deti hai.


### BENEFIT
------------

Database ko source of truth maan kar purani cache copies invalidate kar di jaati hain.
Next subsequent request par Cache Miss hone par latest data Database se fetch kiya jata hai. 
Uske baad required number of cache copies create karke unhe latest data ke saath populate kar diya jata hai.


## PROBLEM
------------

Invalidate karne ke baad next read request ko Cache Miss encounter hota hai,
jiske baad request latest data fetch karne ke liye Database tak jaati hai.

Agar invalidation ke immediately baad bahut saari concurrent read requests
aa jaayen, to multiple requests Database tak pahunch sakti hain aur
Cache Stampede jaisi situation create ho sakti hai.


## IMPORTANT POINT
-------------------

Hot Key Replication me multiple cache keys:

product:101:1
product:101:2
product:101:3

same underlying data ki copies hoti hain.

Isliye Cache Stampede prevent karne ke liye lock individual replicated
cache key ke basis par create karne ke bajaye base/original key ke basis
par create kiya jana chahiye


## 4. CDN / EDGE CACHE
-------------------------

CDN especially useful hai jab Hot Content geographically distributed
users ke dwara access kiya ja raha ho.

Agar Hot Content static ya safely cacheable HTTP response hai,
to usse CDN / Edge Cache par store kiya ja sakta hai.

Isse bahut saari requests Application, Redis aur Database tak pahunchne
se pehle hi CDN se serve ho sakti hain.





============================
## 18 : MULTI-LEVEL CACHING
============================

Multi-Level Caching ka matlab hai data ko ek se zyada caching layers
me maintain karna.


                         REQUEST
                            │
                            ▼
                  ┌───────────────────┐
                  │   LOCAL CACHE     │
                  └─────────┬─────────┘
                            │
                     Cache Hit?
                      /        \
                   YES          NO
                    │            │
                    ▼            ▼
              RETURN DATA   ┌───────────────┐
                            │     REDIS     │
                            └───────┬───────┘
                                    │
                             Cache Hit?
                              /        \
                           YES          NO
                            │            │
                            ▼            ▼
                    POPULATE LOCAL   ┌───────────┐
                        CACHE        │ DATABASE  │
                            │        └─────┬─────┘
                            │              │
                            │       Data Found?
                            │         /      \
                            │       YES       NO
                            │        │         │
                            │        ▼         ▼
                            │   POPULATE    RETURN
                            │    REDIS        404
                            │        │
                            │        ▼
                            │   POPULATE
                            │  LOCAL CACHE
                            │        │
                            └────────┘
                                    │
                                    ▼
                               RETURN DATA


Different cache layers ke different benefits hote hain:

Local Cache
→ Fastest access
→ No network call to Redis or Database

Distributed Cache (Redis)
→ Shared across multiple Application Instances
→ Larger cache capacity
→ Reduces Database calls


Multi-Level Caching ke benefits:

↓ Response Latency
↓ Redis Traffic
↓ Database Load





=====================================
## 19 : CACHE WARMING / PREWARMING
=====================================

Kuch situations me hume pehle se pata hota hai ki kisi particular time
par kuch popular products ke liye bahut zyada traffic aane wala hai.

-------------
### EXAMPLE:
-------------

Black Friday Sale → 10:00 AM

Agar Sale start hone ke time popular products ki Cache entries empty
ya expired hain:

Users
   ↓
Application
   ↓
Cache Miss
   ↓
Database


Ab maan lo kisi ek popular product ke liye bahut saari concurrent
requests aati hain aur sabhi requests Cache Miss encounter karti hain.
Ye requests ek saath Database tak pahunch sakti hain, jisse Database
par sudden load spike aa sakta hai aur Cache Stampede jaisi situation
create ho sakti hai.

Agar ek saath bahut saare different products ki Cache entries bhi
Miss ho rahi hain, to Cache Avalanche jaisi situation create ho sakti hai.

------------------------------
## SOLUTION : CACHE WARMING
------------------------------

Cache Warming / Prewarming ka matlab hai expected-to-be-frequently
accessed data ko actual user requests aane se pehle proactively Cache
me populate kar dena.

Example:

Black Friday Sale start hone wali hai
↓
System identifies popular products
↓
Fetch Data from Database
↓
Populate Redis Cache
↓
Sale Starts
↓
User Requests
↓
Cache Hit
↓
Return Data

Is case me Cache ko populate karne ke liye actual user requests ke
Cache Miss hone ka wait nahi karna padta.

Data pehle se Cache me available hota hai.

---------------------------------
## CACHE WARMING KA MAIN BENEFIT
---------------------------------

Isliye Cache Warming ka main purpose hai:

Agar kisi particular product ke liye **expected high traffic** hai, to uska data pehle hi Cache me populate kar diya jata hai, 
taaki initial requests Cache Miss encounter karke unnecessarily Database ko overload na karein.





=======================================
## 20 : CACHE KEY DESIGN / KEY NAMING
=======================================

Cache me har data ko identify karne ke liye ek unique key hoti hai.

---------------------
## SINGLE PARAMETER
---------------------

Agar request sirf ek identifier par depend karti hai:

### EXAMPLE:
------------

GET /products/101

Cache Key:

product:101

Basic Convention:

<entity>:<id>


------------------------
## MULTIPLE PARAMETERS
------------------------

Agar request multiple parameters par depend karti hai,
to relevant parameters ko bhi Cache Key ka part banana chahiye.

### EXAMPLE:
-------------

GET /products?category=mobile&page=2

Cache Key:

products:mobile:page:2

Basic Convention:

<entity>:<parameter1>:<parameter2>:...


-----------------
### BASIC RULES
-----------------

→ Cache Key unique honi chahiye.
→ Consistent naming convention use karo, otherwise KEY COLLISION ho sakti hai.
→ Relevant parameters ko key me include karo.
→ Keys unnecessarily large nahi honi chahiye.





=======================
## 21 : TTL STRATEGY
=======================

Cache me har data ke liye same TTL rakhna zaroori nahi hota.

TTL ka selection mainly data ki freshness requirement,
change frequency aur access pattern par depend karta hai.

--------------
### EXAMPLE:
--------------

Frequently changing data:

Stock Price → Short TTL

Less frequently changing data:

Product Details → Longer TTL

Rarely changing data:

Configuration → Very Long TTL





=====================================
## 22 : CACHE MONITORING & METRICS
=====================================

Cache ko properly monitor karne ke liye kuch important metrics
track kiye jaate hain.

------------------------
### IMPORTANT METRICS:
------------------------

→ Cache Hit Ratio
→ Cache Miss Ratio
→ Cache Latency
→ Cache Eviction Rate 


-----------------------
### 1. CACHE HIT RATIO
-----------------------

Kitni requests Cache se successfully serve hui.

Higher Hit Ratio
→ Better Cache Effectiveness


----------------------
###2. CACHE MISS RATIO
----------------------

Kitni requests ko Cache me data nahi mila aur backend/Database
tak jaana pada.

Higher Miss Ratio
→ Higher Backend Load


----------------------
### 3. CACHE LATENCY
----------------------

Cache se data return hone me kitna time lag raha hai.

Higher Latency
→ Response time increase ho sakta hai.


----------------------
### 4. EVICTION RATE
----------------------

Kitni Cache entries memory/RAM pressure ki wajah se remove ho rahi hain.

High Eviction Rate
→ Cache ke liye allocated memory (RAM) insufficient ho sakti hai.





=================================
## 23 : WHEN NOT TO USE CACHE
=================================

Har type ke data ke liye Cache use karna zaroori nahi hota.

Cache avoid karna chahiye jab:

--------------------------------------------------------------------
1: DATA FREQUENTLY CHANGE HOTA HO AUR STALE DATA ACCEPTABLE NA HO.
--------------------------------------------------------------------

   Example:
   Stock Price / Live Account Balance

   Kyun?
   Data frequently change hone par har update ke baad Cache ko
   invalidate/update karna padega, jisse unnecessary Cache
   Invalidation overhead badhega.

-------------------------------------
2: DATA BAHUT RARELY ACCESS HOTA HO.
-------------------------------------

   Example:
   Old / Archived Reports

   Kyun?
   Rarely accessed data ke liye Cache ka benefit bahut kam hota hai
   aur Cache ki RAM unnecessarily occupy hogi.

------------------------
3: DATA BAHUT LARGE HO.
------------------------

   Example:
   Large Video Files / Large Reports

   Kyun?
   Bahut large data ko Cache me store karne se limited Cache RAM
   quickly consume ho sakti hai aur frequently accessed useful data
   ke liye available Cache space kam ho sakta hai.
